question:
The treasurer of a mid-sized Toronto bank (CAD balance sheet) must place USD 60 million of a USD liquidity buffer in a single type of instrument for about 11 months. Her criteria are:

- the instrument must have relatively good liquidity, so it can be sold before maturity if needed;
- it must be usable as collateral for borrowing;
- it must offer a higher return than securities issued directly by the US Treasury;
- it may rely on implied government support, but not on the credit of a private bank or corporation alone.

Which instrument best meets all four criteria?
